  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---\ndescription: \"Forked from the official @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-codex: keeps the official one-shot Codex delegation and adds a true-gateway direct connection, queued/steered continuous conversation, live intermediate output, and image passthrough (vision fallback owned by the OCGW gateway system).\"\nkind: \"package-bundle\"\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-subagent-codex-plus",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n**This plugin is forked from the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-codex` plugin**. It keeps the official one-shot Codex delegation exactly as upstream ships it, and layers a set of extensions on top so that **Codex becomes a first-class citizen inside DeepSeek Harness (dsh)**: continuous conversation, live intermediate output, and a true-gateway mode where dsh only relays bytes between you and a Codex session — no model runs in between."
    },
    {
      "section": "Relationship with dsh-subagent-pi",
      "text": "[`dsh-subagent-pi`](https://github.com/february2015/dsh-subagent-pi) is the **sibling plugin** of this one: both are personal forks of the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-codex` that add the same true-gateway layer on top — direct connection, queued/steered continuous conversation, live intermediate output, durable binding, and image passthrough. They differ only in the direct-connected agent — **Codex** here, **Pi** in `dsh-subagent-pi` — and share the same architecture, so features, commands, and docs map one-to-one:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Relationship with dsh-subagent-pi",
      "text": "| | `dsh-subagent-codex-plus` (this plugin) | `dsh-subagent-pi` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Direct-connected agent | Codex | Pi |\n| Lock command | `/codex-lock` | `/pi-lock` |\n| Unlock command | `/codex-unlock` | `/pi-unlock` |\n| Header badge | `CDX-xxxx` | `PI-xxxx` |\n\nBoth projects live under the same GitHub account and are maintained in parallel. Pick either — or install both; each binds its own sessions and they coexist without interference."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. True-gateway direct connection (core)",
      "text": "One local command binds your **current dsh conversation 1:1 to a durable Codex thread**; from then on everything you type in the dsh composer goes straight to Codex — **dsh runs no model in between, it only relays**."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. True-gateway direct connection (core)",
      "text": "- `/codex-lock` binds the session to a persistent Codex thread.\n- `/codex-unlock` unbinds and restores the normal dsh agent loop; the Codex thread is kept and can be rebound anytime.\n- **Durable binding**: after shutting down / restarting dsh, reopening the session auto-reconnects the same Codex thread (connection contention handled automatically), no manual step needed.\n- One Codex thread can be bound to only one dsh session."
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Continuous conversation: queue + direct insert",
      "text": "- While Codex is busy, new messages are **queued** automatically and appear immediately in the native composer queue strip (visible, editable, deletable, steerable), running in order when the current turn ends.\n- The floating panel can **insert** a message directly (it runs ahead of queued messages on the next turn).\n- The queue is fully manageable: the native queue strip can view/edit/delete/steer; the floating panel can insert/cancel."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Live intermediate output",
      "text": "Codex's execution progress (reasoning summaries, message deltas, tool calls, status events) shows up in the dsh session in near real time — not just the final answer. By default it is display-only and never enters the dsh model context.\n\nLong-running tool calls get a **heartbeat**: while a tool item is open, the composer-dock status line shows `正在执行 <tool>` and, after one minute, the live elapsed time (`已运行 4 分 30 秒`). A multi-minute local command therefore never looks like a hang."
    },
    {
      "section": "4. Status display",
      "text": "Once bound, the session header shows a `CDX-xxxx` badge (colored status dot + first 4 thread id chars) and the composer dock shows a \"Codex 直连 · …\" status line. **Unbound sessions show nothing**, keeping the UI clean."
    },
    {
      "section": "5. Image / attachment passthrough",
      "text": "Paste or upload images and hand them to Codex as-is (Codex's own model can see them when it has vision). Vision fallback is handled by the TeamAI skill `ocgw-vision`."
    },
    {
      "section": "6. Delegation and gateway coexist",
      "text": "One dsh conversation can hold multiple one-shot delegated Codex runs (model-triggered) **and** at most one user-attached gateway session, switching freely between them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <name> add /path/to/dsh-subagent-codex-plus\ndsh --profile <name>\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. Open any dsh session (cwd is your project).\n2. Type `/codex-lock`: after binding succeeds the header shows a `CDX-xxxx` badge, and input goes straight to Codex.\n3. While Codex is busy, further messages queue automatically and show up immediately in the native composer queue strip (edit/delete/steer), running in order when the current turn ends.\n4. `/codex-unlock` disconnects; the Codex thread is kept and can be rebound anytime."
    },
    {
      "section": "Delegation (official baseline, unchanged)",
      "text": "```yaml"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh profile settings",
      "text": "- id: tool-subagent-codex\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\n  config:\n    provider: codex-plus\n    toolName: subagent_codex\n    backgroundMode: one-shot\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Docs",
      "text": "- `IMPLEMENTATION.md` — feature checklist (implementation details)\n- `REQUIREMENTS.md` — requirements spec\n- `TECH-VERIFICATION.md` — technical verification report (implementation technology)"
    }
